{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/623300-beast-the-city-of-no-illusions-actual-play","id":623300,"title":"Beast: The City of No Illusions (Actual Play)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-11T07:59:00-07:00","id":623300,"title":"Beast: The City of No Illusions (Actual Play)","content":"I\u2019m about to start a short Beast chronicle using the Kickstarter rules preview. A couple of my players were very excited and anxious to do it, so I couldn\u2019t wait for the rules to be officially released.<br /> We met to create characters on the 1<sup>st</sup>, but a couple of the players have been preparing them for much longer than that! It\u2019s been kind of a fragmented process, since not everyone made it to the creation session and it started late so we had to end early. Long story short, it\u2019s totally possible that all the PCs won\u2019t know each other to begin with, which is something I\u2019m actually ok with! I do regret the lack of group-setting discussion\u2026<ul><li>Tricia\u2019s character is <b>Lyudmilla</b> (Eshmaki Nemesis). She\u2019s a 19 year old runaway in a Puerto Rican girl gang. Her parents are undocumented immigrants from eastern Europe, but she\u2019s very much an American girl. Her Horror is a huge black dog with a skull head. She generally feeds by punishing people who abuse their power. Her prophetic nightmares let her serve as her gang\u2019s bruja, but since being Devoured she\u2019s been struggling with whether or not she should stay with them.</li> <li>Josie will be playing <b>Shiloh</b> (Makara Nemesis). She was Devoured in 2005 when she was 15, so she\u2019s been a Beast for her entire adulthood. Her parents always pushed her to succeed at everything she did, which led her to a good college on the coast and a great career overseas as a high-powered administrative assistant. She used her position to find and punish people for their entitlement, but her disconnection to the broader monstrous community has recently left her feeling unfulfilled. She\u2019s moved back home to try and reconnect with the life she left behind. Her horror is a cecaelia (octopus mermaid) with an anglerfish\u2019s lure.</li> <li>Chucky\u2019s character is <b>Cale Belisario</b> (Eshmaki Predator). An up and comer in the local organized crime scene, his branch of the family was framed for disloyalty and wiped out. He survived and wants revenge against those who framed him\u2014he doesn\u2019t blame the bosses who actually gave the order. He really believes in the family and his highest aspiration is to put the house back in order. During the day-to-day he\u2019s a grafter, a thief, and a monster that teaches honor among thieves.</li> <li>Andrew\u2019s character is <b>Dave Jackson</b> (Eshmaki Collector). He\u2019s a very talented but hard on his luck artist. His own landscape paintings (based on what he saw in his disturbing dreams) sell poorly. He\u2019s also a capable forger, but the paintings he replaces go into his collection, which is a bad way to meet the rent. Oh, also he\u2019s a thrill-seeker, and spends what little cash he has going hiking, climbing, and sky-diving, trying to reproduce the thrill of flying that he used to have in his dreams. His Horror is a golden, fire-breathing dragon.</li> <li>Melissa plays <b>???</b> (Makara Nemesis). She\u2019s a skilled veterinarian who cares deeply about animals and punishes people who abuse them. Alongside her medical work, she\u2019s also political mover and fund-raiser. Her Horror is a classically beautiful Greek siren.</li> </ul>I wanted to talk about what city it would be in, but I\u2019d been previously thinking about using Buffalo, NY, so when we were running short on time I pitched that and people seemed fine with it (Tricia previously lived in Buffalo so she was particularly tickled to play in it).<br /> I\u2019ve still got some work to do with the characters; Melissa needs a name, Chucky needs a solid Horror, a couple still need more fleshing out, and most of them need connections to each other and to NPCs. This coming week I\u2019ll make a post about my plans for the first session and the rest of the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T08:47:38-07:00","id":623353,"title":"","content":"Looking forward to seeing how this goes. Best of luck; some cracking concepts there!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T13:20:57-07:00","id":625793,"title":"","content":"Planning and random thoughts! <b>Players: please don't open spoiler tags!</b><br /> <br /> Buffalo is a city of disparate pieces living in relative harmony. Walking down a block can practically transport you from one world to another. Safe, rich streets butt up against gang territory and adjacent neighborhoods have totally different, starkly defined cultures.<br /> <br /> Buffalo is also a city struggling to reclaim its golden years, redefining itself, polishing its iron and glass face, but unable to completely rid itself of rust. Gangs, human and monstrous, vie for territory and fifteen thousand abandoned buildings provide ample cover for things that prefer to not be seen.<br /> <br /> People in Buffalo are used to taking the good with the bad. It\u2019s hard not to when you can drive down the street and see both laid out in front of you. They understand what kind of a place they live in, and any who can\u2019t cope with that dual nature move away before too long. But a Beast\u2019s sight pierces further, and sees the terrors behind the day-to-day. For Beasts, Buffalo is truly a City of No Illusions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Both Lyudmila and Shiloh were devoured by the same Beast (inspired by the Ludiaeg from the October Daye series). I\u2019m not sure if she\u2019s the Apex yet. I want her to be powerful, possibly Incarnate, but reclusive and less interested in other monsters than in Beasts.<br /> <br /> Looking at the characters, there are some pretty clear trends. Nemesis, nemesis, nemesis. Eshmaki, Eshmaki, Eshmaki. Mobster, gangster, criminal. I think one of the themes is going to be crime and punishment. What makes something a crime? What gives someone the right to punish?<br /> <br /> <br /> So let\u2019s think about the supernatural scene in Buffalo. Tricia wants Lyudmila to associate with Werewolves, several players thought it made sense for them to have Vampiric contacts, and Melissa was particularly interested in Changelings. Nobody seemed interested in Mages, and while I love them, I\u2019m relieved to be able to mostly exclude them. There was also some interest in Sin-Eaters and Prometheans. I may also end up including Princesses, since my previous game was a year-and-a-half Princess chronicle.<br /> <br /> <br /> My gut instinct is to represent the rich vs poor aspect of Buffalo as Vampires vs Werewolves. But honestly, there are Vampires on both sides of the fence (Werewolves, too, but it\u2019s less of a trend). So let\u2019s focus on having two factions of Vampires. Invictus with ties to mortal organized crime is definitely one. The obvious opposition would be Carthians, but I think the Circle would work better due to its potential ties to the Dark Mother. The other three covenants <i>exist</i> in Buffalo, but don\u2019t have as strong a presence.<br /> <br /> Werewolves fit in well with the street gangs. We want one near Lyudmila, so probably a neighboring gang. I could see a more religiously-minded pack being aligned with the Circle (though probably looked down on by the other packs). I\u2019ll need to take another look at my map of Buffalo neighborhoods while I think about this. [Dave\u2019s bar fight might be made to relate to Werewolves somehow]<br /> <br /> Changelings, huh. Well, first, I want to use some of the new ideas about Court creation, even if we don\u2019t\u2019 quite have all the rules for it to make sense. The different Courts that spring to mind are Light (Buffalo was one of the first cities with electricity, and it\u2019s called the City of Light), Water (the river and falls are pretty important), Iron (the industrial revolution was a big deal), and Rust. I think Rust is a relatively new Court that started forming in the 70s and had been gaining strength as the others, especially Iron, declines. Not a particularly subtle metaphor but that\u2019s OK. Light and Water are strongly allied. Light is loosely supportive of Iron. Rust isn\u2019t allied with anyone, but isn\u2019t <i>enemies</i> with Light and Water. It makes sense elementally for Rust and Water to be associated, but it wouldn\u2019t look good, so perhaps it\u2019s an underhanded alliance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I think I\u2019ve decided that the Apex of the area is an Oneiromancer from the Court of Rust. At the behest of their king, they\u2019ve spread a lot of subtle influence directly into Buffalo\u2019s dreamscape, and the Primordial Dream reflects that. They\u2019re the one who framed Cale\u2019s family as part of an attempt to destabilize the mob, because the mob is on the opposite side of the \u201ceconomic revival\u201d spectrum.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":". 10-02-2015, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T22:27:09-07:00","id":626338,"title":"","content":"Very cool - I really like as you hammer the PCs base themes in game and reflect them in the supernatural societies the Begotten can dwell in Kinship with - like Covenants choosing or building Fae Courts. I will mark this technique for mine games using Beasts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T06:10:25-07:00","id":626536,"title":"","content":"This makes me very happy. I'll be watching. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T19:09:46-07:00","id":628169,"title":"","content":"Seems promising!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T02:14:17-07:00","id":642766,"title":"","content":"Here here! Can't wait to see how this Chronicle will develop. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> May I suggest also implementing elements of the other game lines core themes to reflect the city as well? Some example might be:<br /> <br /> Who we are tonight (Requiem 2E): The future for most of the Begotten is dark and unknowable so how do they chose to be one a nightly/daily basis? How do the people of Buffalo chose to live in an environment as such?<br /> <br /> The Wolf Must Hunt (Forsaken 2E): The Begotten must hunt as well, how do they reconcile their existence? What meaning do they bring to their condition? What of the other predators of Buffalo. After all the Devouring might have felt frighteningly like a Homecoming to some of the Begotten. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Beautiful Lies, Bittersweet Truths (Lost 2E): The Primordial Dream and the World of Darkness are but a distant trickle of water or a faulty lightbulb away at certain places. How do the Begotten distinguish between their regular lives and pursuit of furthering their Legend. What lies do they see all around them? What lies don't they see, do they not see it conveniently? What is the grim truth about life in Buffalo for both mortal and supernatural beings? <br /> <br /> Hope that helps. XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-01T09:01:13-07:00","id":684508,"title":"","content":"So it's been absolutely <i>forever</i>, but the chronicle is slowly moving forward. We've only had two sessions so far, and we'll be having another on the 10th. I'm still working on the session summary, but here's some of what I've got done for now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Meetings and Introductions: Chapter One</b></span><br /> <br /> An average weekend. Saturday, August 15th, 2015.<br /> <br /> Dave Jackson is in his studio, working on a new painting. He\u2019s trying, really trying, to discard years of intuition and experience. Rent is coming due, and he <i>needs</i> to sell something. But an hour later, when he steps back and squints, he sees the signs: a cloud that looks like a skull, rivers of viscera stretching across a fleshy plain. It\u2019s perfect, he can\u2019t imagine how to fix it. No sane person will buy it. People sleeping near these things get awful nightmares. Dave sighs. He needs a drink.<br /> <br /> Cale Belisario, Mafioso extraordinaire, is on the hunt. He\u2019s prowling through wretched hives of scum and villainy, looking for his prey of choice. He doesn\u2019t hunt criminals, he\u2019s another step up the food chain. He hunts thieves who steal from thieves. The wendigo that only eats cannibals.<br /> <br /> Lyudmila the Young Queen is dining with her fellow royalty. Cheap wings and cheaper beer. She left her family name and it\u2019s foreign blood behind. She\u2019s 100% American hellhound and she runs with a gang of furies. The only all-female gang in Buffalo and their miserable slice of East side. Their leader, Maria Ortez, is a transplant from NYC, here to start a new franchise of Young Queens.<br /> <br /> <br /> Three Beasts walk into a bar.<br /> <br /> Well, not all at once. Lyudmila was here first, The Queen City is her gang\u2019s place. They all but own it, and the staff is glad for the business and security, even if it means occasionally catering to the whims of young, dangerous women. Cale came in around sundown and chose a seat where he could watch the rest of the patrons. Finally, Dave enters.<br /> <br /> The Eshmaki notice each other, tasting heritage through the smoke. They tamp down their reactions, and Dave continues to the bar to get a drink.<br /> <br /> The bartender has it ready before he sits down, shaking his head with amusement. Dave smiles at him and sips his screwdriver. He\u2019s been coming here for a week or two now and the bartender is finally getting the hang of using mixers. It\u2019s kind of a dive, and he doesn\u2019t really know anyone here, but he likes the atmosphere. The boisterous attitude of the girls on the balcony (Dave is vaguely aware that they must be some kind of gang) is contagious, and the other people here have a familiar, down-on-their-luck air about them. They\u2019re his kind of people, all things considered.<br /> <br /> The door opens. Four guys walk in. Young, tough looking men. The atmosphere changes immediately. They hold themselves in formation, like soldiers in enemy territory. Their body language is overbearing and they practically sneer at the patrons. They <i>don\u2019t belong</i>. The Beasts get a whiff of them, two are human, the other two have a feral scent, like watered-down Werewolf They walk toward the back, toward the stairs up to the balcony.<br /> <br /> Dave stands up as the thugs pass him. \u201cExcuse me,\u201d he says politely.<br /> <br /> One of the humans puts a hand on his shoulder and shoves him back onto his stool. \u201cShut up and sit down.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was just wondering what you\u2019re doing here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWho the fuck are you, asshole? Stay out of it and finish your drink.\u201d<br /> <br /> Upstairs, the Young Queens have noticed the change in mood below. They all look down and see the guys walking toward them. None of them seem to have any gang colors or signs. Lyudmila identifies two of them as Wolf-blooded, mostly humans who have some of the powers of Werewolves and often have a role in their packs. Maria narrows her eyes, then stomps toward the stairs, with Lyudmila the rest of the Queens behind her. The two groups meet at the bottom of the stairs.<br /> <br /> Cale pays Satiety and activates From the Shadows, turning invisible, and sneaks up behind the group. Gang war is absolutely a violation of honor among thieves. He spends Satiety and hits one of the wolf-blooded with You Cannot Run. The ganger pales, aware that the whole bars attention is on his group. He shrinks back, then forces his way past his allies, running for the door. To everyone else, it looked like he ran away as soon as he saw Maria. The leader shakes his head, then turns back to Maria. <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">He probably shouldn't have been able to do that, given the target couldn't see him...</span></span><br /> <br /> \u201cWho the fuck are you and what the fuck do you want?\u201d She growls.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is your warning, bitches. Clear out. This isn\u2019t your territory anymore.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd what if we don\u2019t?\u201d Lyudmila retorts.<br /> <br /> The thug cracks his knuckles. \u201cWell, I wasn\u2019t looking forward to hurting a bunch of little girls,\u201d he shrugs, \u201cbut I figured I might have to.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck that!\u201d With a flash, Maria pulls her knife and slashes at the wolf-blood, scoring a deep cut across his chest. He snarls and starts to draw, when Lyudmila raises her arms and begins chanting in ululating Ukrainian. To most of those present, it may as well be Tongues. She looks deep in the leader\u2019s eyes and uses All Your Teeth Are Falling Out. The wolf-blooded catches a glimpse of her Horror, a canine skull suddenly imposed on her face.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">She rolled an exceptional success, but after some checking of the rules I found out that she can\u2019t add this as a Chamber because it isn\u2019t Foggy or, uh, Disruptive. :\u2019(</span></span><br /> <br /> He flinches back, eyes wide and trembling. \u201cWhat the fuck?\u201d He mumbles, feeling his teeth shift in his mouth. He reaches up and catches a glimpse of his withered hand. \u201cWhat the fuck!? The fuck did you do to me!?\u201d<br /> <br /> Lyudmila and the rest of the girls grin at him, sharp and predatory.<br /> <br /> He staggers back, pointing and shouting. \u201cThis is your only warning, get it? We\u2019re just the messengers!\u201d He gasps, wheezing, then runs for the door. The two humans exchange a terrified look, then follow.<br /> <br /> Cale, still invisible, sneaks behind the bar, grabs a bottle of high-proof whiskey, and jogs out after them. Dave, also decides to follow. Lyudmila asks Maria if she can be excused.<br /> \u201cShit, I dunno why you\u2019d wanna leave after that performance! But, sure, go ahead.\u201d<br /> <br /> As Lyudmila walks out after Dave, Maria announces that drinks are on her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":". 10-02-2015, 03:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T12:49:35-07:00","id":686060,"title":"","content":"<b>Meetings and Introductions, Chapter One (cont)</b><br /> <br /> Shiloh is playing prodigal daughter. She\u2019s gotten an apartment downtown, a car, even a job. But now it\u2019s time to stop putting off the whole reason she came back. First stop on her journey of self-discovery is her Elder Sister, who she sometimes has trouble not thinking of as her Sire, despite the vast cultural difference. The Makara drives down to the waterfront, to the apartment building that Carrie lives in.<br /> <br /> The building <i>isn\u2019t</i> abandoned. It\u2019s clearly being taken care of, if not well. It still has heat and electricity. Just\u2026 no one lives there anymore. No one but Carrie.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s on the third floor. Shiloh walks up the stairs, feeling conspicuous in the low-rent building. It\u2019s been a long time since she\u2019s spent any time in the gutter. She rings the doorbell and waits, anxiously. Normally, she\u2019s cool and collected, but this is outside her day-to-day. Which is kind of the point.<br /> <br /> Carrie answers the door. She\u2019s a short, older woman, somewhere between middle and old age. She\u2019s a sharp contrast to Shiloh\u2019s youth and glamour.<br /> <br /> \u201cShiloh,\u201d she says, apparently nonplussed, \u201cI never expected <i>you</i> to visit. Come in.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shiloh does, the pull of the invitation as irresistible as the pull of Carrie\u2019s whirlpool Horror.<br /> <br /> The two Beasts make some small talk, but the conversation quickly comes around to why Shiloh is back in town. Shiloh tells her elder sister that she\u2019s looking to reconnect with her monstrous heritage. Carrie recalls that Shiloh used to run with a brood of younger vampires, and recommends trying to find them.<br /> <br /> They\u2019d called themselves the Young Bloods. Three kindred\u2014Carlos, Veronica, and Gloria\u2014and Shiloh. Four monsters from different walks of life, none of them quite adults. They were barely a coterie and no one took them seriously. The vamps had all been turned too young or barely old enough, and only had a couple years of nightlife on them. Shiloh fit in perfectly. Then she left them behind when she went to college, and barely thought of them when she chased her career overseas. <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Carlos and Gloria were Gangrel and Veronica was a Mehket.</span></span><br /> <br /> \u201cAre they even still alive?\u201d It was almost a miracle they\u2019d survived long enough for her to leave.<br /> <br /> Carrie shrugs. \u201cMaybe, maybe not. Good for you either way.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Goal in mind, the Makara heads back to her apartment to change, then walks downtown to the rack. The best way to find her friends, she reasons, is to ask around.<br /> <br /> Despite its run-down Eastside, Buffalo has a thriving nightlife downtown, especially on the weekend. It\u2019s bigger, brighter, and louder than Shiloh remembers, but she\u2019s not sure if this is a sign of growth and revitalization, or the convulsions of a dying city. She moves through the crowds with grace and precision, turning heads as she goes.<br /> <br /> Sure enough, after checking out a couple clubs, she finds a pretty large group of vampires. She approaches and introduces herself, making it clear that she\u2019s not kine. They introduce themselves as Tyesha, Bruce, Verde, Venom, and Alta. They\u2019re friendly, if slightly suspicious (thanks, Thicker than Water!), and out for a night of unwinding, not feeding. They only start looking predatory when Shiloh asks them about the Young Bloods. <span style=\"color:#0000ff\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Tyesha and Alta are Daeva, Verde and Venom are Gangrel, and Bruce is a Nosferatu.</span></span><br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe we know something, maybe not. Get a drink, sit a while, I\u2019m sure we can work something out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shiloh reluctantly does so. She chills with them for a while, making sure to casually touch each one and learn something about them with Mimir\u2019s Wisdom. <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Another mistake, because she wasn\u2019t at low satiety\u2026</span></span> After about an hour or so, she gets Tyesha alone and whispers the vampire\u2019s secret. Tyesha\u2019s face clenches.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s your intention?\u201d She demands.<br /> <br /> Shiloh remains cool. \u201cSame as when I walked in. You tell me what I want to know, no one hears about this.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tyesha grimaces. \u201cFine,\u201d she spits, \u201chere\u2019s the deal: your friends are dead. Carlos and Veronica got ripped apart by werewolves years ago. The other one skipped town. Happy?\u201d<br /> <br /> She\u2019s telling the truth. Shiloh frowns. \u201cNot really, no.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cToo bad, bitch. Now get the fuck out of here and don\u2019t come back. I see you around here again, I\u2019ll drain you dry. Got it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Shiloh holds up her hands in sarcastic surrender and does as she\u2019s told.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Mechanically, I wanted to put Leveraged on Shiloh in exchange for the info. She then put Leveraged on Tyesha with Mimir\u2019s Wisdom, which canceled it out. Wore out her good impression by being so blunt, though.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T09:09:22-07:00","id":688400,"title":"","content":"This looks interesting. I feel kinda sorry for Shiloh already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Da